[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   step_15: formal model comparison + the last standard-physics controls.
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   M1  ecliptic-latitude control: the axis sits at beta ~ -13 deg, so
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   in-cap aphelia are preferentially low-|beta|.  If the excess
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   were ecliptic-proximity (deeper planetary-plane scattering),
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   matching the |beta| distributions must kill it.  Compute the
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   cap contrast inside |beta| strata and on a |beta|-matched
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   subsample.
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   M2  patch-model likelihood: d_of ~ baseline + A * exp(-theta^2/2 s^2)
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   fitted on the CODE-only data vs the flat null -> likelihood
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   ratio / BIC-based Bayes factor.  One number for the patch.
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   M3  auxiliary class-2 sample: class 2a/2b CODE-only comets --
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   lower-quality orbits the anomaly should still touch if it
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   lives in the sky rather than in orbit quality.
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   M4  seasonal/solar-longitude control: if the excess were an
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   observation-geometry artifact tied to discovery season,
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   d_of should correlate with solar longitude at perihelion,
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   not with the fixed axis.  Uses perihelion year+month from
[2026-09-21 14:36:09 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 038]   the catalogue epoch.
